// A RANGE'S VIEW IS LIVE FROM ITS FIRST BOUND (DEF-410 (e), landing 176). The emitter loads a List's or a buffer's
// header (items and count; ptr and len) BEFORE the range's bounds run (`emit_range_slice`), so a bound that
// reallocates the container through `@l` or `$$m l`, or swaps the buffer through `@b`, left the view pointing at
// the FREED buffer: `l[0...(raw grow(@l))][0]`, the view's `.len`, the view as an argument, the view stored in a
// slice local -- each read the allocator's poison (230) or a stale count on landings 174 and 175 with no verdict
// (`.internal/t176/census/e/`, `ev_range_grow`, `ev_range_grow_buf`). The range's VIEW party is raised before its
// bounds are walked (`acc_indices` pushes `push_value_view_parties` ahead of the bound walk; the chain's own
// access skips its party, `chain_passes_through`) and every write-capable access inside the bounds is judged
// against it (BORROW-015). An inline array ranged (stable storage) and a slice parameter re-pointed read the
// fresh elements in fact and are refused all the same (sites 7, 8): the named-view twin (`int64[]:v = g[0...2];
// drop resetg(@g); v[0]`) is D-325's refusal, and a window is judged as the view it is. Plain bounds, a bound
// that only READS (`count_of(@l)`, `$$i l`), a write THROUGH a range step and a range handed to a writer of it
// are the legal twins (`tests/backend/programs/range_bound_window_ok.npk`). A bound that MOVES the List is
// MOVE-001 by the bindings analysis first (DEF-410 (a)); `string_bytes(s)[0...(raw grows(@s))]` and a view
// handed to a callee under a reallocating bound were BORROW-015 before this landing (D-325, face (b)). Sites 9 and 10 (176b,
// review B's E1): the growth in the INDEX of a range view and in the bound of a range OVER a range view -- `acc_indices` walks
// a chain bottom-up in emission order now, a range step's party raised where its header loads (top-down, 176 walked the outer
// index before reaching the range under it: the view read the freed buffer, 230); the safe mirror, the growth in an index UNDER
// the range step (`l[(raw push_row(@l))].v[0i64...2i64][1i64]`, refused by 176 as B-R1), is the `_ok`'s case 6.
mod:range_bound_window;
error:E5;
func:grow = int64(List<int64>->:p) never fails { for (int64:i in 0i64...200i64) { drop list_push(p, i); } pass 1i64; };
func:swap = int64(buffer->:p) never fails { (<-p) = buffer_new(64i64); (<-p)[0i64] = 98u8; pass 1i64; };
func:resetg = int64(int64[2]->:p) never fails { (<-p) = [1i64, 2i64]; pass 9i64; };
func:repoint = int64(int64[]->:p, int64[]:other) never fails { (<-p) = other; pass 9i64; };
func:peek = int64(int64[]:v) never fails { pass v[0i64]; };
func:mk_list = List<int64>() never fails {
    List<int64>:l = raw list_init::<int64>(2i64);
    drop list_push(@l, 7i64);
    drop list_push(@l, 8i64);
    pass l;
};
